\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.11}{\ignorespaces Empirical local epoch allocation dynamics under severe statistical heterogeneity (Dirichlet label skew $\alpha =0.5$), illustrating the closed-loop setpoint tracking dynamics of FDA-RoLoRA on MNLI and QNLI under Dirichlet label skew ($\alpha =0.5$).}}{56}{figure.5.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.12}{\ignorespaces Convergence and client drift variance trajectories on MNLI and QNLI under severe Dirichlet statistical heterogeneity ($\alpha = 0.5$). Top panels present validation accuracy trajectories; bottom panels present client coordinate drift variance ($\sigma _t^2$).}}{56}{figure.5.12}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.13}{\ignorespaces Empirical Setpoint Tracking Dynamics in FDA-RoLoRA: In IID regimes, super-linear coordinate variance growth causes steady-state undershoot ($\mathcal {S} \approx 0.64\text {--}0.79$); in Non-IID regimes, near-linear drift allows the controller to accurately track the nominal setpoint ($\mathcal {S} \approx 0.91\text {--}1.11$).}}{59}{figure.5.13}%
